From c911c2e5cb14b5ea23bf7830e41908e082907dae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Reilly <jreilly1821@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:58:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] installer: Report failures, support a distro post-install
 unit, enroll the installed disk

- An installation that systemd-sysinstall fails is now reported on the
  install page ("Installation Failed" and the error) instead of moving on
  to the recovery key and done pages.
- pages.conf can name a template unit in [page:installer]
  post-install-unit=, e.g. distro-post-install@.service. After
  systemd-sysinstall succeeded, setup starts it with the target disk as
  the instance (systemd-escape --path) and waits for its job; a failure is
  reported like an installation failure. This lets a distribution finish
  what a block copy cannot do by itself (new filesystem UUIDs, boot entries,
  crypttab, firmware entries) before the recovery key page wipes the empty
  passphrase.
- The recovery key page enrolls the key on the LUKS2 partition of the disk
  the OS was installed to (from the udev database), falling back to
  /dev/disk/by-label/root, which may also name the live medium's root.

Signed-off-by: James Reilly <jreilly1821@gmail.com>
